course: dictionary
lesson: 5899
title: Where words come from
level: primary-5
stars: 0
explain: Some words travel from one language to another. When you meet a word that sounds unusual, ask where it comes from. Marathi is a language spoken by about 80 to 100 million people, mainly in the state of Maharashtra in western India, including the city of Mumbai.
explain: Marathi can be a noun or an adjective. As a noun it names the language and its people, so you might read «speak Marathi». As an adjective it describes things from Maharashtra, like «Marathi film» or «Marathi food».
explain: The word «mongoose» comes from Marathi. Its origin tells you how to spell its plural: «Mongoose comes from Marathi, a language of India, so its plural is mongooses.» It has nothing to do with goose, so it does not become «mongeese».
fact: Marathi is a language spoken mainly in the state of Maharashtra in western India.
fact: Marathi is written in the Devanagari script, the same script as Hindi.
fact: Marathi speakers live all over the world, including in the UK, the USA and Australia.
fact: «Mongoose» comes from Marathi, a language of India.
fact: Knowing where a word comes from can help you spell its plural, as with «mongooses» and «moose».
exercise: «Mongoose comes from Marathi, a language of India, so its plural is mongooses.» What language does mongoose come from? | *Marathi | English | Algonquian | Hindi
exercise: Which state of India is Marathi mainly spoken in? | Punjab | Kerala | *Maharashtra | Gujarat
exercise: Which city is in the area where Marathi is mainly spoken? | Sydney | *Mumbai | Paris | Glasgow
test: When Marathi is an adjective, what does it describe? | Only the words in a dictionary | *The people, culture or things of Maharashtra | Sounds made by birds | Weather in the Scottish hills
test: Which script is Marathi written in? | Cyrillic | Greek letters | *Devanagari, the same script as Hindi | Arabic
exam: Why is the plural of mongoose «mongooses», not «mongeese»? | *Because mongoose comes from Marathi, so it has nothing to do with goose | Because it is spelled with a goose inside | Because it always has two of everything | Because it is a Native American word
